1431
04:53:02,610 --> 04:57:03,160
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: And after considering the objections of the chair of the respondent, the objection is hereby denied subject to the following guidelines. and reasonings. Section 34, Rule 132 of the Rules of Court provide the court shall consider no evidence which has not been presented or formally offered. The purpose for which the evidence is offered must be specified accordingly. The marking, identification, or authentication of a document does not mean that the document has been formally offered or admitted for the purpose it was so stated. The physical transfer of an exhibit designation from a provisional copy to its corresponding original or certified true copy is even more limited. It is a mechanical and ministerial act intended only to maintain the orderly identification of the Court's records. The respondent is not prejudiced by this transfer. The transfer does not alter the substance or evidentiary status of the document . It does not constitute a ruling on the authenticity, admissibility, or evidentiary weight and it does not enlarge the purpose for which the document was originally marked. The respondent therefore loses no substantive or procedural right by reason of the transfer and may raise all appropriate objections when the document is formally offered. This conclusion is consistent with the prosecution's own representation during the July 21, 2026 hearing wherein the Honorable Luistro stated, quote, Your Honor, the document is being presented only to seek confirmation from the witness. that he is referring to this particular document as part of the investigation of the Special Task Force. We are not presenting it to prove the truthfulness of the contents of the affidavit. The Chair likewise previously ruled, quote, Again, this is only as to the fact that this is what the NBI used in their open investigation and coming up with their findings, not as to the truth of the statements being read by Director Matibag. Close quotation. The Chair further clarified on even date, July 21, 2026. The Chair will cut short any further identifications of the witness in regard to this affidavit. This is only as to the fact that Las Cañas executed a document that they used in their open source investigation, not as to the truth of what was said. The limitations remain controlling even after the transfer of the marking of this exhibit to a certified true copy. Exhibits P-4-35, 35A, and 35B remain merely independently relevant statements only to establish that the document came to the attention of and was used by the NBI in its investigation. It may not be used as proof of the truth of the allegations stated therein. As stated in Espinelli v. People, GR No. 79-535, dated 6-9-14, when the relevant fact is merely that a statement was made, the hearsay rule does not bar proof of that fact, regardless of the statement's truth or falsity. Finally, the transfer of the markings does not cure the defects already placed on the record. The purported affidavit remains unsigned unauthorized and not made under oath with no witness having attested to its execution and truth of its contents. The contents of the affidavit at this time remain hearsay, the transfer of the markings notwithstanding to a certified true copy of that document. Accordingly, the Clerk of the Impeachment Court is directed to set the requested conference as requested I think this afternoon. If I'm not mistaken, at 4 p.m. Now, the motion for judicial notice. The chair will make a ruling, will grant the motion with a reminder, a stern reminder and warning.

